    <node id="metmastery_product">
      <data key="d0">MET Mastery (product)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">.playwright-mcp/page-2026-09-03T18-46-11-311Z.yml</data>
      <data key="d3">landing page</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Sibling MET-prep product (diagnostic + study plan + teacher tools); '© 2026 MET Mastery'. Distinct from the mock-test-2 simulator but shares the six MET skills and CEFR/B2 framing.</data>
      <data key="d4">9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="metmastery_diagnostic">
      <data key="d0">MET Mastery Diagnostic</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">.playwright-mcp/page-2026-09-03T18-46-11-311Z.yml</data>
      <data key="d3">Find my starting point</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">One diagnostic yields a provisional B2-level picture across the six MET skills with per-skill percentages.</data>
      <data key="d4">9</data>
    </node>
    <node id="metmastery_learning_loop">
      <data key="d0">Learning Loop (6 steps)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">.playwright-mcp/page-2026-09-03T18-46-11-311Z.yml</data>
      <data key="d3">THE LEARNING LOOP</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Six-step loop: Diagnose -&gt; Target gap -&gt; Build exam rhythm -&gt; Remember lesson -&gt; Read feedback -&gt; Ask teacher; keeps human teacher in the loop for writing/speaking nuance.</data>
      <data key="d4">9</data>
    </node>
