      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Provisional, honest scoring: shows the learner's starting point across the six MET skills before spending time practising what they already know (sample dated 12 May).</data>
      <data key="d4">92</data>
    </node>
    <node id="page-2026-09-04T07-22-28-659Z_learning_loop">
      <data key="d0">Learning Loop (6-step method)</data>
      <data key="d1">code</data>
      <data key="d2">.playwright-mcp/page-2026-09-04T07-22-28-659Z.yml</data>
      <data key="d3" />
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Design principle stated verbatim: 'Good preparation is not a pile of random questions. It is a loop: find the gap, work on it, get useful feedback, and try again.' Steps: Diagnose first, Target the gap, Build exam rhythm, Remember the lesson, Read clear feedback, Ask your teacher.</data>
      <data key="d4">92</data>
    </node>
