    <node id="dka_skill">
      <data key="d0">Dispositional Knowledge Assessment Designer</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">src/education-skills/skills/original-frameworks/dispositional-knowledge-assessment-designer/SKILL.md</data>
      <data key="d3">line 89</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Dispositional knowledge exists only in enactment; rubrics rate a fixed trait and can undermine motivation via evaluative feedback. Assessment must make the disposition VISIBLE through multi-informant evidence (teacher observation, student self-reflection, optional parent input) over time, not measure it via summative judgment.</data>
      <data key="d4">71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="lta_skill">
      <data key="d0">Learning Target Authoring Guide</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">src/education-skills/skills/original-frameworks/learning-target-authoring-guide/SKILL.md</data>
      <data key="d3">line 82</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Mandatory Knowledge Type classification (Type 1/2/3) determines the assessment instrument BEFORE band statements are written; this prevents the most common failure mode in competency curricula — dispositional goals assessed through rubrics (illusion of measurement).</data>
      <data key="d4">71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="panel_review_skill">
      <data key="d0">Panel Review (Seven-Role Independent Mode)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">src/education-skills/skills/professional-learning/panel-review/SKILL.md</data>
      <data key="d3">line 68</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Gate rule (mean_overall&gt;=88 AND no role mean&lt;70) prevents a single role's sustained dissent (e.g. therapeutic-education sceptic) from being averaged into passage — the floor is a structural blocker, not a number to be averaged away.</data>
      <data key="d4">71</data>
    </node>
    <node id="knowledge_types">
      <data key="d0">Knowledge Type Classification (Type 1/2/3)</data>
      <data key="d1">document</data>
      <data key="d2">src/education-skills/skills/original-frameworks/learning-target-authoring-guide/SKILL.md</data>
      <data key="d3">lines 115-159</data>
      <data key="d10" />
      <data key="d11" />
      <data key="d12" />
      <data key="d13" />
      <data key="d14">Type 3 dispositional knowledge requires multi-informant longitudinal observation (NO RUBRIC); Type 1 hierarchical -&gt; rubric/knowledge test; Type 2 horizontal -&gt; reasoning-quality rubric. The classification determines the assessment route.</data>
      <data key="d4">71</data>
    </node>
